1vn9|n|To break at once; to break short, as substances that are brittle. ; To strike, to hit, or to shut, with a sharp sound. ; To bite or seize suddenly, especially with the teeth. ; To break upon suddenly with sharp, angry words; to treat snappishly; -- usually with up. ; To crack; to cause to make a sharp, cracking noise; as, to snap a whip. ; To project with a snap.	N:ryc,45,1~ryc,45,1
1vn9|a|To break at once; to break short, as substances that are brittle. ; To strike, to hit, or to shut, with a sharp sound. ; To bite or seize suddenly, especially with the teeth. ; To break upon suddenly with sharp, angry words; to treat snappishly; -- usually with up. ; To crack; to cause to make a sharp, cracking noise; as, to snap a whip. ; To project with a snap.	j:ryc,55,2~ryc,55,2
1vps|n|A small part or piece.	n:djq,80,6~djq,80,6
